<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Independent Social Democratic Party of Germany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as USPD</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Independent Social Democratic Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> (USPD) was formed in 1917 by socialists who broke with the Social Democrats over support for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It played a leading role in the revolution of 1918–1919 and in council governments such as that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a>. In 1920 most of its members joined the Communists, and the rest rejoined the Social Democrats in 1922.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/independent-social-democratic-party-of-germany.jpg" alt="Independent Social Democratic Party of Germany" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dahn · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USPD_logo,_1920.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
